WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.780
Managing intrinsic load begins with sequencing.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.860
Learners usually benefit from moving from simple to complex,

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.270
from prerequisite knowledge to combined performance,

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.665
and from clear examples to more varied cases.

00:00:10.665 --> 00:00:13.305
When instruction begins with the full complexity of a task,

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:16.920
beginners may not know which elements matter or how the parts relate.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.520
Sequencing gives them a path into the domain.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.220
Chunking and scaffolding help learners handle complexity.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.975
A chunk groups related information into a meaningful unit.

00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:27.720
A scaffold provides temporary support while the learner builds capability.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.280
In practice,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.900
this might mean teaching one decision rule before combining it with exceptions,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.720
showing one data flow before introducing multiple systems,

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.300
or giving learners a checklist before expecting fluent independent performance.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.060
Worked examples and partially completed examples are especially useful early.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.435
They reduce the need for learners to discover every step while they are still forming the

00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:46.440
basic schema.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.585
A worked example shows how a task is solved and why the steps matter.

00:00:49.585 --> 00:00:52.985
A partially completed example asks learners to finish selected parts,

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:56.819
which shifts some responsibility to them without dropping all support at once.

00:00:56.819 --> 00:00:59.040
Progressive complexity is the key.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.835
Reduce the number of interacting elements early, then add more as learners gain structure.

00:01:02.835 --> 00:01:04.800
This does not mean hiding reality forever.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.320
It means building foundations before expecting full independent performance.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.090
When learners have a stable starting model,

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.740
later complexity becomes easier to place and less likely to overwhelm working memory.
